{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTowerBridge"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent.one_not_mem_either","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent.one_not_mem_either","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TLTowerRadicalDescent.lean#L123-L134","doc":"**Non-vacuity: the unit escapes both radicals** when `τn 1 ≠ 0`. The upper\nstatement is the interesting one — it says the induced trace on `Hn1` is not\nidentically zero on the image, which is what stops\n`map_mem_traceRadical` from being a statement about the whole algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent.map_mem_traceRadical_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent.map_mem_traceRadical_iff","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TLTowerRadicalDescent.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**The tower inclusion detects the radical exactly.**\n\nBoth directions together. This is the statement that makes the quotients a\n*tower*: the induced map `Hn / rad τn → Hn1 / rad τn1` is injective, so `TL_n`\nsits inside `TL_{n+1}` rather than merely mapping to it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent.mem_traceRadical_of_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent.mem_traceRadical_of_map","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TLTowerRadicalDescent.lean#L86-L102","doc":"**And reflects it.** The converse of `map_mem_traceRadical`: if `ι a` is in\nthe upper radical then `a` is in the lower one.\n\nThis direction is where `retract` is spent. A test element `b : Hn` is lifted to\n`ι b : Hn1`; the hypothesis applied there gives `τn (a * ε (ι b)) = 0`, and\n`ε (ι b) = b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent.map_mem_traceRadical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TLTowerRadicalDescent.map_mem_traceRadical","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TLTowerRadicalDescent.lean#L68-L84","doc":"**The inclusion carries the lower radical into the upper one.**\n\nIf `a` pairs to zero against all of `Hn`, then `ι a` pairs to zero against all of\n`Hn1` under the induced trace — because `ε` moves the test element back down:\n`τn1 (ι a * x) = τn (ε (ι a * x)) = τn (a * ε x) = 0`.\n\nThe conditional expectation is doing the work. Without it the statement is not\nmerely unproved but unstateable: nothing would relate a test element of `Hn1` to\none of `Hn`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}